---
// PROTOTYPE: what this is, for whom, and on what principles.
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
---
<Site title="About | Germany on AI" description="What Germany on AI is, who it is for, and the principles it follows.">
  <section class="intro">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Germany on AI is a situation report on German AI policy for advocates, researchers, journalists and
      officials who need to find their way around it quickly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="what">
    <h2><a class="self" href="#what">What it is</a></h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        It collects what Germany says and decides on AI in the Bundestag and government, in the European
        Union and at the UN and other international bodies. The situation report shows recent events, the
        calendar ahead and the bills still open. Analysis and interpretation will appear in a separate,
        versioned report.
      </p>
      <p>
        Others track parts of this ground too; their work is listed under
        <a href="../method/#catalogue-others">Method and sources</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="principles">
    <h2><a class="self" href="#principles">Principles</a></h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <ul>
        <li>Every item links to its original public source.</li>
        <li>Figures are counted by stated rules, and the same data always gives the same result.</li>
        <li>Records are kept as their sources published them. Interpretation is labelled and kept separate.</li>
        <li>Only people in public roles are named, in their official capacity.</li>
        <li>Corrections are welcome and recorded.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="who">
    <h2><a class="self" href="#who">Who is behind it</a></h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Built and maintained by Lennart Klein as an independent project. Code is published under the MIT
        licence, data under CC BY 4.0.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">Contact details and funding statement to be added before publication.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>
